# Where fw_setenv finds the U-Boot environment.
#
# It is the file U-Boot itself writes with saveenv, on the shared FAT
# partition, which is what makes the two halves of the A/B mechanism talk
# to each other at all: U-Boot decrements a counter here at boot, and RAUC
# resets it here from Linux once the slot is marked good.
#
# THE SIZE MUST MATCH U-BOOT'S CONFIG_ENV_SIZE EXACTLY. It is not a maximum
# and nothing checks it. Too small and fw_setenv writes a short environment
# that U-Boot reads as corrupt, falling back to its built-in defaults,
# which resets BOOT_ORDER and both counters and quietly undoes every
# decision the update system has made. Too large and it writes past the
# end of the environment into whatever the FAT filesystem put next.
#
# 0x4000 is the value in the rpi_arm64 defconfig. If U-Boot is ever
# rebuilt from a different configuration, this number is the first thing
# to check and the last thing anything will warn about.
#
# Device name      Device offset   Env. size
/boot/uboot.env    0x0000          0x4000
